cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ref-build: scRNA reference-dataset builder for RCTD (spacexr) — primary + donor pool → adaptive migration → 10X-style mtx bundle → Reference .rds"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "xenium-preprocess-pipeline contributors"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-09"
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.PLACEHOLDER"                    # TODO after Zenodo mint
url: "https://example.org/ref-build"
repository-code: "https://example.org/ref-build"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - scRNA-seq
  - reference-dataset
  - RCTD
  - spacexr
  - SPLIT
  - spatial-transcriptomics
  - celltype-annotation
abstract: >-
  ref-build is step 3 of the Xenium spatial-data preprocessing
  pipeline. It takes a primary sample's preprocessed scRNA AnnData and a
  pool of same-primary-tumor-type donor scRNA AnnData files, applies
  per-celltype adaptive migration rules (rule 1: primary-
  only when the primary's cell count for a celltype > 100; rule 2:
  borrow from donors that HAVE the missing celltype; the intermediate
  case supplements the primary via donor-balanced sampling capped at
  the primary's per-celltype count), emits a per-celltype
  audit-trail CSV, writes a 10X-style {counts.mtx, features.tsv,
  barcodes.tsv, metadata.csv} bundle, and finally shells out to
  Rscript to build the spacexr::Reference .rds object that RCTD's
  create.RCTD consumes as its reference side. Adapted from an
  internal SPLIT/Proseg workflow.
